{"kind":"assert","text":"R14 retirement decisions (ruling 7d5cbfcf point 2; closes the\ninventory step of 6dd06d03 section 2.3). Inputs: the static inventory\nat Main 61fc3e3d (docs/security/entry-points.md, the three Worker\nconfigurations), the first complete usage report dbf7e6bd (30 days to\n2026-10-27T13:00Z: dap-grow 128,921 weighted route events, dap-demo\n227, artroom-scope 422, dap-lending no telemetry), and the first\ncensus and version reports of 19:36 (c676a6c7). Zero observation\nnominates; observed use rules out; the record decides.\n\nOne reading governs the route list. The route meter (measuredRequest,\npackages/scope/src/operational.ts) wraps the outer HTTP request and\nreturns serve() unmeasured inside an operational context, and the\nhosted MCP reaches the scope operations through route() in process\n(packages/scope/src/worker.ts:846). So an operation the hosted MCP\ncalls is never a route place of its own. Zero-observed HTTP places are\nnot zero use.\n\nRetire (two builder requests under this parent, filed now):\n1. The ScopeService entrypoint (worker.ts:670). No deployed Worker\n   binds it: the sandbox binds ApplicationScreenService; the test\n   configurations bind NetService, PlatformService and the serving test\n   services. The page and the MCP routes call api(env.SCOPES) directly\n   (self-hosting note, section 4.1). Five test files reference it.\n2. The legacy GitHub demo context in packages/scope/src/demo-creation.ts\n   (LegacyGitHubDemoContext, legacyGitHubDemoConfig, the fixed origin set\n   of artroom-scope and artroom-rehearsal) and the fixed origin constant\n   that apps/room/demo-creation.ts:19 compares. artroom-scope is retired\n   for creation since 2026-10-23 and the rehearsal Worker no longer\n   exists. The current offer keeps its v2 form; its origin comes from\n   the deployment's own setting, not a constant.\n\nKeep, decided by design:\n- The GitHub port (outsideOf, worker.ts:526). No Worker configures it\n  today (no GITHUB setting in any configuration) and it is selected\n  only for a scope whose recorded host is github.com. It is the\n  github.com shape of the Git host choice note (053c5595) and the port\n  that G3 bind-repository uses. Not retired.\n- Artifacts: bound on all three Workers and the register host of every\n  hosted room. METRICS: bound on grow and demo, absent on lending, the\n  source of this report. APPLICATION_CONTENT (R2): bound on grow and\n  artroom-scope only, the retained-file store (retained 9,347 events\n  on grow). Each is per configuration now, not bound regardless of it.\n  Console logs at full sampling on grow and demo are a sink decision\n  of the observability design (2026-10-12), not a retirement.\n- Zero-observed HTTP places on all three Workers (application-\n  projection, items, outboxItem, requests, reservation-snapshot, settle,\n  site, stream): settle and reservation-snapshot are the settlement\n  path landed this window and called by the hosted MCP; items, outbox\n  and application-projection are called by the hosted MCP in process\n  and by the CLI; requests is read by the CLI status report; site is\n  read by the room page and the CLI; stream is consumed by the client\n  library's head stream (the counter app) and by the application\n  sandbox through the named RPC exchange, which bypasses the route.\n  None is retired. The stream's public HTTP route is the one candidate\n  to revisit when the single-node runtime's stream matter is decided\n  (ruling 46852be4).\n- Native platform versions: governed by definition succession and K1\n  (ruling point 2); the version reports of 19:36 are the first pin\n  census (grow destination@12 directory@16 inbox@1 membership@8\n  register@17 rules@10; lending destination@2 directory@5 inbox@1\n  membership@4 register@5 rules@3). No retirement from usage.\n\nWith these two requests filed, the inventory step of 2.3 is decided.\nR14 bb763efa closes when the two heads land. No further usage runs\nunless the metric shape changes."}